# The opening day in Russian: проснувшись, улыбаясь, открыв дверь
subtitle: "Проснувшись в пять, надев фартук, спеша и улыбаясь: Tom writes up the opening day of «Кухонька» with Russian gerunds, the way written Russian tells a day."
tags: ["russian","russian gerunds","verbal adverbs","russian writing","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/gerunds","writing/essays"]
thumb: "band \"Tell a day in Russian\" stamp \"5 ДЕКАБРЯ\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Reading Gogol in Russian: Christmas Eve","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/220-russian-gogol-christmas-eve.cast"}

